Short answer: the method generalises, the constants do not. And one parity fact first, because it changes the question.
Degree arithmetic
For a polynomial speed w, the curve is r' = w^2, so deg r = 2*deg w + 1. Degree 5 is deg w = 2; the next PH curve is degree 7 (deg w = 3). A polynomial PH curve of degree 6 does not exist — even degrees are impossible, because w^2 is always even-degree and integration adds one. So "6th order" would have to mean a rational speed, or a degree-6 approximation to a degree-7 curve.
