• Even cleaner: If you set \(t \in [0, 1]\) with \(N = 25\) (\(n = 5\)) and scale by \(3125\), every single triangle has exact integer legs and an exact integer hypotenuse:
	• Step 1 (\(i = 0\)): \(\Delta x = \mathbf{+1249}\), \(\Delta y = \mathbf{+50}\), \(\Delta s = \mathbf{1250}\)
	• Step 2 (\(i = 1\)): \(\Delta x = \mathbf{+1241}\), \(\Delta y = \mathbf{+150}\), \(\Delta s = \mathbf{1250}\) (Wait: \(1241^2 + 150^2 = 1540081 + 22500 = 1562581 \neq 1250^2\); for exact integers on a \(3125\) grid over \(t \in [0, 1]\), \(N=5\) gives denominator \(2 \times 125 = 250\), and \(N=25\) gives denominator \(2 \times 15625 = 31250\).)

